§ 9-1.   Reapportionment of wards.
There shall continue to be seven wards in Upper Dublin Township, which wards
are hereby reapportioned to be as nearly equal in population as practicable
based on the official statistics of the 2020 Federal Census conducted by the
United States Census Bureau.
§ 9-2.   Retention in office and new elections.
The commissioners in office at the time of this reapportionment shall retain
their offices and continue to represent their respective wards until the end of
their respective terms. The election of commissioners under the reapportionment
shall be held in accordance with the First Class Township Code, 53 P.S. § 55101
et seq., and the Pennsylvania Election Code, 25 P.S. § 2600 et seq.
§ 9-3.   Boundaries of the First Ward, Ward One.
The boundaries of the First Ward shall be as shown on the Electoral District
Ward Map, dated May 10, 2024 and prepared by Katherine Stein, which is on file
and is available for public inspection in the office of the Township Secretary,
the legal description thereof being as follows:
   ALL THAT CERTAIN political block or voting district known as Ward One,
situate in the political subdivision known as Upper Dublin Township, Montgomery
County, Commonwealth of Pennsylvania, said Ward being located in the southwest
corner of the Township, being bordered to the north by the Borough of Ambler
and Lower Gwynedd Township; to the west by Whitpain Township; and to the south
by Whitemarsh Township, and being bound and described as follows, to wit:
   BEGINNING at point in the centerline of Cedar Road and Loch Alsh Avenue;
THENCE from said point of beginning extending southeasterly along the
centerline of Loch Alsh Avenue, crossing the beds of Hoffman Road, Lake Drive,
Honey Run Creek and Farm Lane to the centerline of the Route 309 Expressway;
THENCE extending southerly along the centerline of the Route 309 Expressway to
the centerline of Highland Avenue; THENCE extending southeasterly along the
centerline of Highland Avenue, crossing the beds of Fort Washington Avenue,
Summit Avenue, Madison Avenue, Hartranft Avenue, Pinetown Road and the Sandy
Run Creek to the centerline of Camp Hill Road; THENCE extending southerly along
the centerline of Camp Hill Road, crossing the beds of the Virginia Drive,
Pennsylvania Turnpike, the Norfolk Southern Trenton Cutoff Railroad and
Dreshertown Road to a point, said point being the common Upper Dublin Township
and Whitemarsh Township line; THENCE extending northwesterly along said common
township line, crossing the beds of the Norfolk Southern Trenton Cutoff
Railroad, the Pennsylvania Turnpike and the Route 309 Expressway, then entering
the bed of Pennsylvania Avenue, crossing the beds of Commerce Drive, Summit
Avenue, Fort Washington Avenue and North Bethlehem Pike, leaving the bed of
Pennsylvania Avenue and continuing along the common township line, crossing the
beds of the Wissahickon Creek and entering the bed of Morris Road, crossing the
beds of Mill Spring Drive and Fir Road, leaving the bed of Morris Road and
continuing along the common township line, crossing the beds of Beech Road,
Carey Drive and Butler Pike to a point, said point being a point on the common
Upper Dublin Township and Whitpain Township line, said point also being on a
point of the common property line between Tax Block 35, Units 23 and 41; THENCE
extending northeasterly along the said common township line, crossing the beds
of Morris Road, the Wissahickon Creek and West Maple Street to a point, said
point being a point on the common Upper Dublin Township, Whitpain Township and
Borough of Ambler line; THENCE extending along the Borough of Ambler line, in a
counter-clockwise manner, in the following 12 courses:
      (1)   Southeasterly, crossing West Maple Street,
      (2)   Southwesterly, to an angled point,
      (3)   Southerly, crossing Butler Pike to an angled point,
      (4)   Southeasterly, paralleling the Wissahickon Creek and Morris Road to
an angled point within the extended centerline of West Church Street,
      (5)   Northeasterly, crossing the SEPTA Railroad to the center of the
Church Street and Main Street intersection,
      (6)   Southerly, along the centerline of Main Street to the centerline of
Randolph Avenue,
      (7)   Easterly, along the centerline of Randolph Avenue to a point,
      (8)   Northerly, leaving Randolph Avenue to an angled point,
      (9)   Northeasterly, paralleling Church Street to the centerline of
Ambler Road,
      (10)   Northwesterly, along centerline of Ambler Road to the centerline
of Church Street,
      (11)   Northeasterly, along the centerline of Church Street, crossing the
beds of Southern Avenue, Highland Avenue, Trinity Avenue and Rosemary Avenue to
the centerline of South Bethlehem Pike,
      (12)   Northerly, along the centerline of South Bethlehem Pike, crossing
the beds of Mattison Avenue and Lindenwold Terrace to the centerline of Ardross
Avenue;
   THENCE extending easterly along the centerline of Ardross Avenue, crossing
the bed of Douglas Street to the centerline of Cedar Road; THENCE extending
northeasterly along the centerline of Cedar Road to the centerline of Loch Alsh
Avenue, the point and place of beginning.
   Intending to describe the perimeter of a political block or voting district
in Upper Dublin Township known as the First Ward.
§ 9-4.   Boundaries of the Second Ward, Ward Two.
